    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "36a0d2c1_a56f3e14",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/btm_sco.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 259,
      "author": {
        "id": 1079709
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-12T06:45:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"as many SCO packets as possible\" could be misleading.\nIf I understand it correctly, below while(1) should generate the #of mSBC frames as close to what just received in payloads.\n\nAnd it\u0027s not too late we document the schedule scheme thoroughly. should cover:\n1. the role of btm_route_sco_data(). works between SCO and audio server\n2. in transaction between each layers, there should be same amount of data give and take",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 258,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 259,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "3d53722df234f09ad7ac2a8e2b8f2169ca8bf990",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe2400d4_3e6ca146",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/btm_sco.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 259,
      "author": {
        "id": 1543626
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-13T09:46:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added the comment on https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/2184725/3. PTAL.\n\nWe may use more tuning to assure the read/write balance between each layers.\n\nThe currrent implementation focuses more on assuring the read and written data amount are the same between the BT daemon and the audio server. This can keep the data rate stable if we can assure the audio server can always recieve and send the amount of data the BT daemon requests. However, if audio server fails to do so, we\u0027ll rely on the adapter to balance the read/write data.\n\nThe alternative solution will be focusing on the data balance between the BT daemon and the adapter, so that we\u0027ll assure we write a packet to the adapter whenever we read one. For this solution, we\u0027ll rely on the audio server to handle solve the read/write inbalance whenever a read/write from/to the audio server failed. \n\nPlease help advised.",
      "parentUuid": "36a0d2c1_a56f3e14",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 258,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 259,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "3d53722df234f09ad7ac2a8e2b8f2169ca8bf990",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
